<title>UK: Tuskar rig spuds in Obe oil field off Niger Delta.</title>
<headline>Tuskar rig spuds in Obe oil field off Niger Delta.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tuskar Resources Plc has started drilling at its development well in the Niger Delta, off Nigeria, the company said on Friday.</p>
<p>The Obe-4 well was spudded by the jack-up rig Glomar Adriatic X on June 24 in a water depth of about 67 feet.</p>
<p>Drilling at the appraisal well is expected to take about 30 days with testing commencing shortly after.</p>
<p>The Obe oil field is in the north-eastern part of the OML 110 offshore concession which covers 240,000 acres.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 8980</p>
</text>
